  "arrangerNotes": "Chorus, vocal line, transcribed by visual reading of the original 1917 Will Rossiter sheet music (scan and LilyPond transcription saved in scores/b9/scan/), key C major, 4/4, starting on the pickup; second ending taken. Simplifications (chromatic passing and neighbour notes played as the nearest drum note): the two F sharps ('ready', 'two-steps') are played as 4, the two G sharps ('ready', 'play the') as 5, and the C sharp before 'goin' to dance' as 1'. D drum: as written (range 1 to high 3), D minLayout 13. C drum: the C drum has no high 2/3, so 'goin' to dance out both my shoes' and 'Darktown Strutters' Ball' (from 'at the') are played one octave lower; C minLayout 11. The title and lyrics are kept as published in 1917. 'Darktown' is a period term, now considered dated and offensive, for an African-American neighbourhood; it is kept here only because it is the song's published title. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
}
